## Development Install

Run straight from source with `go run`, which always reflects the current code, so there's no built binary or installed extension to go stale between edits:

```bash
go run ./cmd/{{ project_name }} [args]
```
{%- if use_goreleaser %}

To test the actual `gh {{ project_name }} ...` extension invocation or a Homebrew install, use the released version rather than installing from this checkout:

```bash
gh extension install {{ repository_namespace }}/{{ project_name }}
# or
brew install --formula {{ repository_provider }}/{{ repository_namespace }}/{{ project_name }}/raw/main/Formula/{{ project_name }}.rb
```
